{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('index.html');s=p.read_text().replace('</style>','''@media(max-height:500px) and (min-width:561px){#title{padding:62px 6vw 40px}.titlecopy{width:47%}.titlecopy>.eyebrow,.titlebadge,.decorlabel,.boardcaption{display:none\"'!important}h1{font-size:62px;margin:0 0 12px;line-height:.8;letter-spacing:-1px}.subtitle{font-size:12px;line-height:1.4;max-width:320px;margin:0 0 12px}.titleactions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;max-width:340px;gap:7px}.titleactions .primary{grid-column:1/-1;min-height:39px;padding:9px 13px}.titleactions .secondary{font-size:15px;min-height:35px;padding:8px 9px;gap:5px}.titleactions .secondary .buttonhint{display:none}.minorlinks{margin-top:13px;gap:20px}.textbutton{font-size:10px}#topbar{padding-top:16px}.brand{font-size:18px}#footer{bottom:12px;letter-spacing:.7px;font-size:8px}.panel h2{font-size:32px}.panel .setting{margin:12px 0}.panel .primary,.panel .secondary{min-height:39px;font-size:19px}}\n</style>'\"''');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('main.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"phase='title';mode='solo';online.leave();\\\", \\\"phase='title';toastTime=0;\"'$('\"'#toast').style.opacity=0;mode='solo';online.leave();\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"buildScene();disposeWorld();loadStage(0);setupInput();setPrompts();\\\", \\\"buildScene();disposeWorld();loadStage(0);if(navigator.maxTouchPoints>0)lastInput='touch';setupInput();setPrompts();\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Super Bounceout\n\nGood angles. Bad intentions.\n\nAn original ink-and-paper arcade brick breaker inspired by Super Breakout (1981).\nThe complete four-stage run features Classic, Cavity, Double and Progressive rules,\narmored bricks, captive balls, three pickups, piercing ink bursts and shared-world co-op.\n\n## Play\n\nOpen the HTML in the parent folder in a current browser. The Three.js r180 engine,\nTSL shaders, Rapier 0.19.3 code and physics WebAssembly are embedded in that file.\nThe fonts download if available, with local fallback fonts. Cross-device online rooms\nload PeerJS 1.5.5 on demand and use its public signaling service; same-device tabs use\nBroadcastChannel. AI Hub sessions use only the supplied Hub client and transport.\n\n- Move: left stick / D-pad, mouse, A/D or arrows. On touch, drag anywhere on the board.\n- Serve / next stage: Cross, A, Space, click or tap.\n- Ink burst at 100%: Triangle, Y, Shift, right click, two-finger touch or the burst button.\n- Pause: Options, Escape, P or the menu button.\n- Local player two: second controller or arrow keys; player one uses A/D or mouse.\n- Title attract mode begins after 10 seconds idle; any input exits.\n- Pause → Developer tools exposes live balance sliders, infinite balls, AI, stage skip,\n  multiball, burst fill and reset. Music starts at 10%.\n\n## Build and check\n\nFrom this directory:\n\n\"'```\nnpm run build\nnpm test\n```\n\nThe tests own an OS-selected loopback port and close their own browser/server resources.\nThe single test command prints failures and one count line. It covers real physics,\na natural AI run through all four stages, controls, touch, audio, networking and the\nsupplied Hub conformance harness, including dedicated-server and packet-loss cases.\n\n`visual_check.py` creates screenshots for manual layout inspection. Its `?webgl` URL\nuses the renderer'\"'s WebGL2 fallback to obtain nonblank screenshots on headless machines;\nthe game and automated engine checks default to WebGPU.\n\n\"'`main.js` owns data-driven stages, gameplay, UI, native AnimationMixer effects and controls.\n`audio.js` synthesizes every sound and voice. `online.js` owns session/room transport.\n`credits.json` supplies the in-game source information and feedback. `build.mjs` bundles\nall code and inserts the unmodified Hub session client as the first head script.\n\nThe root `exit-interview.json` is the machine-readable catalogue and production record.\nEOF\nnode build.mjs\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python visual_check.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('index.html');s=p.read_text().replace('</style>','''@media(max-height:500px) and (min-width:561px){#title{padding:62px 6vw 40px}.titlecopy{width:47%}.titlecopy>.eyebrow,.titlebadge,.decorlabel,.boardcaption{display:none\"'!important}h1{font-size:62px;margin:0 0 12px;line-height:.8;letter-spacing:-1px}.subtitle{font-size:12px;line-height:1.4;max-width:320px;margin:0 0 12px}.titleactions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;max-width:340px;gap:7px}.titleactions .primary{grid-column:1/-1;min-height:39px;padding:9px 13px}.titleactions .secondary{font-size:15px;min-height:35px;padding:8px 9px;gap:5px}.titleactions .secondary .buttonhint{display:none}.minorlinks{margin-top:13px;gap:20px}.textbutton{font-size:10px}#topbar{padding-top:16px}.brand{font-size:18px}#footer{bottom:12px;letter-spacing:.7px;font-size:8px}.panel h2{font-size:32px}.panel .setting{margin:12px 0}.panel .primary,.panel .secondary{min-height:39px;font-size:19px}}\n</style>'\"''');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('main.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"phase='title';mode='solo';online.leave();\\\", \\\"phase='title';toastTime=0;\"'$('\"'#toast').style.opacity=0;mode='solo';online.leave();\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"buildScene();disposeWorld();loadStage(0);setupInput();setPrompts();\\\", \\\"buildScene();disposeWorld();loadStage(0);if(navigator.maxTouchPoints>0)lastInput='touch';setupInput();setPrompts();\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Super Bounceout\n\nGood angles. Bad intentions.\n\nAn original ink-and-paper arcade brick breaker inspired by Super Breakout (1981).\nThe complete four-stage run features Classic, Cavity, Double and Progressive rules,\narmored bricks, captive balls, three pickups, piercing ink bursts and shared-world co-op.\n\n## Play\n\nOpen the HTML in the parent folder in a current browser. The Three.js r180 engine,\nTSL shaders, Rapier 0.19.3 code and physics WebAssembly are embedded in that file.\nThe fonts download if available, with local fallback fonts. Cross-device online rooms\nload PeerJS 1.5.5 on demand and use its public signaling service; same-device tabs use\nBroadcastChannel. AI Hub sessions use only the supplied Hub client and transport.\n\n- Move: left stick / D-pad, mouse, A/D or arrows. On touch, drag anywhere on the board.\n- Serve / next stage: Cross, A, Space, click or tap.\n- Ink burst at 100%: Triangle, Y, Shift, right click, two-finger touch or the burst button.\n- Pause: Options, Escape, P or the menu button.\n- Local player two: second controller or arrow keys; player one uses A/D or mouse.\n- Title attract mode begins after 10 seconds idle; any input exits.\n- Pause → Developer tools exposes live balance sliders, infinite balls, AI, stage skip,\n  multiball, burst fill and reset. Music starts at 10%.\n\n## Build and check\n\nFrom this directory:\n\n\"'```\nnpm run build\nnpm test\n```\n\nThe tests own an OS-selected loopback port and close their own browser/server resources.\nThe single test command prints failures and one count line. It covers real physics,\na natural AI run through all four stages, controls, touch, audio, networking and the\nsupplied Hub conformance harness, including dedicated-server and packet-loss cases.\n\n`visual_check.py` creates screenshots for manual layout inspection. Its `?webgl` URL\nuses the renderer'\"'s WebGL2 fallback to obtain nonblank screenshots on headless machines;\nthe game and automated engine checks default to WebGPU.\n\n\"'`main.js` owns data-driven stages, gameplay, UI, native AnimationMixer effects and controls.\n`audio.js` synthesizes every sound and voice. `online.js` owns session/room transport.\n`credits.json` supplies the in-game source information and feedback. `build.mjs` bundles\nall code and inserts the unmodified Hub session client as the first head script.\n\nThe root `exit-interview.json` is the machine-readable catalogue and production record.\nEOF\nnode build.mjs\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python visual_check.py'","aggregated_output":"Super-Bounceout-Super-Breakout-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-011153.html (2.45 MB)\n{\"state\": {\"phase\": \"playing\", \"mode\": \"solo\", \"stage\": 0, \"score\": 50, \"lives\": 3, \"charge\": 8, \"combo\": 0, \"burst\": 0, \"wideTime\": 0, \"slowTime\": 0, \"elapsed\": 5.475000000000062, \"balls\": 1, \"remaining\": 46, \"renderer\": \"WebGL2 fallback\", \"physics\": \"Rapier 0.19.3\", \"three\": \"180\", \"stats\": {\"brickHits\": 2, \"paddleHits\": 2, \"lostBalls\": 0, \"powers\": 0, \"bursts\": 0}, \"settings\": {\"music\": 0.1, \"sfx\": 0.65, \"glyphs\": \"ps\", \"shake\": true, \"assist\": false}, \"config\": {\"speed\": 11, \"paddleWidth\": 3.1, \"chargeRate\": 1, \"god\": false, \"auto\": true}, \"ballState\": [{\"x\": 2.7969093322753906, \"y\": -3.8794102668762207, \"vx\": 1.0871390104293823, \"vy\": 10.946146965026855, \"docked\": false}], \"paddles\": [{\"x\": 2.4082439909498787, \"y\": -9.6, \"seat\": 0, \"width\": 3.1}], \"metrics\": {\"frames\": 29, \"steps\": 657, \"renderErrors\": 0}}, \"errors\": []}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
